   "text": "“How should a child of noble family who wishes to practise the profound perfection of wisdom train?” This is what he said, and the noble Avalokiteśvara, the bodhisattva and great being, replied to venerable Śāriputra as follows: “O Śāriputra, a son of noble family or daughter of noble family who wishes to practise the profound perfection of wisdom should regard things in this way: They should see the five aggregates to be empty of nature."
  },
